    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="0888" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg808"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCreery to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1357.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the embassy’s No. 1274 of
                    February 21 last, forwarding a copy of the report of the third circuit judge,
                    showing that the case of Nathaniel F. Bonsall, who complained of unreasonable
                    delay in his trial, was being conducted in accordance with law, I have the honor
                    to inclose a copy of the ambassador’s letter to the assistant general manager of
                    the Sonora Railway inquiring the status of the case.</p>
                <p>I inclose a copy of Mr. Naugle’s reply, stating that Mr. Bonsall, being afraid he
                    might be imprisoned, went to Texas; and forwarding a communication from Attorney
                    Eduardo Viñas (copy herewith), stating that the above-mentioned court sentenced
                    Mr. Bonsall to eight months’ imprisonment and that amparo proceedings were
                    instituted against the sentence.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fenton R.
                    McCreery.</hi></signed></closer>




